            "response_snippet": "You can use the following Lucene query to retrieve active connection strings in the Solr index using the `secret_keys` override parameter:\n\n```\n?q=(*OR*active_connection_string:*))&rows=0&wt=json&fl=connectionString\n```\n\nHowever, if you want to use the `override` parameter with the value `'secret_keys'`, you will have to use the Solr query syntax which is slightly different from the Lucene one.\n\nAssuming that your Solr index is using the schema less configuration and the field names match exactly with your collection's fields, you can run a query like this:\n\n```\nGET /your_collection/params?fl=connectionString&rows=0&wt=json\n?override=secret_keys\n```\n\nPlease note that `secret_keys` override parameter works by prefixing all values in `connectionString` field to the prefix specified in `override=secret_keys` parameter. This means, if you want to get actual connection strings, this query will not return anything because of the nature of the override mechanism.\n\nTo actually retrieve active connection strings, you would need to use a different query syntax that takes into account the presence of some other field like `active_connection_string`.",
