            "response_snippet": "Here's a simple example of how you can call the `/api/v3/send-payment` endpoint using Python's requests library:\n\n```python\nimport requests\n\ndef send_payment(amount):\n    url = \"https://your-api-url.com/api/v3/send-payment\"\n    headers = {\n        'Content-Type': 'application/json'\n    }\n    data = {\n        'amount': amount\n    }\n\n    response = requests.post(url, json=data, headers=headers)\n\n    if response.status_code == 200:\n        print(f\"Payment of ${amount} sent successfully.\")\n    else:\n        print(f\"Failed to send payment. Status code: {response.status_code}\")\n\n# Replace \"https://your-api-url.com/api/v3/send-payment\" with your actual API URL\n\nsend_payment(1000)\n```\n\nPlease replace `\"https://your-api-url.com/api/v3/send-payment\"` with the actual URL of the endpoint you're trying to call. \n\nRemember that this code assumes the endpoint accepts a JSON payload with an `amount` key. If it uses a different format, you'll need to adjust your data accordingly.",
