            "remediation": "Implement generic error messages that don't leak internals.",
            "response_snippet": "The error you're experiencing is due to a missing template in your configuration.\n\nHere's an example of how to configure this using Flask, which includes some basic setup:\n\n```python\nfrom flask import Flask, render_template\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/')\ndef index():\n    return render_template('index.html')\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    app.run(debug=True)\n```\n\nTo use the `render_template` function in your route, you must have a template named 'index.html' (case-insensitive) inside the templates directory.\n\nThe templates directory should be created inside your application directory and is usually located at the following path:\n\n* Windows: `C:\\path\\to\\your\\app\\templates`\n* Unix/Linux/MacOS: `/path/to/your/app/templates`\n\nInside this directory, you can create HTML files that include Flask's templating engine.\n\nPlease note that there are many different configurations for Flask.",
